---
title: Quick Calamari with Garlic Mayonnaise
description: Simple but moorish shallow-fried squid rings
source: Nigella Express <urn:isbn:9780701181840>
author: Nigella Lawson
servings: 4
prep time: 15m
cook time: 15m
course: Starter
locale: en_GB
difficulty: Medium
tags:
- seafood
- savoury
- starter
---

> Double quantities to serve as a main course.

= Garlic Mayonnaise =

Grate or crush the @garlic{0.5%clove} into the @mayonnaise{100%g} and stir to mix.

= Calamari =

Heat the @groundnut oil{250%ml}(or as needed depending on size of pan) in a smallish saucepan and, while it is left to warm up, cut the thawed @frozen squid, tubes and tentacles{500%g} into 1 cm rings.

Put the @cornflour{2%tbsp}, @semolina{4%tbsp}, @salt{1%tsp}, and @paprika{1%tsp} into a plastic freezer bag.

Add the squid rings and tentacles and then toss to coat.

When the oil is hot enough, which is when it sizzles up fiercely when you drop in a small cube of bread, fry the squid in batches to get the most golden crunchiness. ~{2%minutes} per batch is all you should need.